1
00:00:00,658 --> 00:00:02,998
What if your salary showed up on a public ledger,

2
00:00:03,038 --> 00:00:04,473
for anyone to read?

3
00:00:04,513 --> 00:00:06,809
On Monad today, it does.

4
00:00:07,654 --> 00:00:10,539
Kakushi comes from builders who think a payment on a public

5
00:00:10,579 --> 00:00:13,349
chain shouldn't publish your salary, your customers,

6
00:00:13,389 --> 00:00:14,722
or your balance.

7
00:00:15,324 --> 00:00:18,500
Every Monad payment shows who paid, who got paid,

8
00:00:18,540 --> 00:00:20,253
and how much. Payroll,

9
00:00:20,293 --> 00:00:23,658
merchants and OTC desks can't work like that.

10
00:00:24,248 --> 00:00:28,144
Why now? Monad's sub-second finality makes private payments

11
00:00:28,184 --> 00:00:31,700
practical, and payment apps are launching on it right now.

12
00:00:32,372 --> 00:00:33,957
Kakushi does three things.

13
00:00:33,997 --> 00:00:36,070
Hide who. Hide how much.

14
00:00:36,110 --> 00:00:37,629
Add it to any app.

15
00:00:42,608 --> 00:00:44,498
It's live on testnet:

16
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:47,014
44 verified contracts,

17
00:00:47,054 --> 00:00:51,624
a stealth receipt in 431 milliseconds and finality in about

18
00:00:51,664 --> 00:00:55,505
a second, the full FHE flow on chain,

19
00:00:55,646 --> 00:00:57,742
a Monad to Sepolia bridge,

20
00:00:57,782 --> 00:01:00,729
and a six-deposit pool our team seeded.

21
00:01:01,573 --> 00:01:05,155
It's for Monad wallets, payment apps and payroll apps,

22
00:01:05,195 --> 00:01:08,595
and they add it with a drop-in widget and an SDK.

23
00:01:09,474 --> 00:01:12,383
Kakushi. The privacy provider for Monad:

24
00:01:12,423 --> 00:01:16,336
ZK hides who, FHE hides how much.

